# Baseline Kubernetes PodSecurity hardening deferrals for scim-app-k8s.
# All CRITICAL checks and 22+ other HIGH Kubernetes misconfiguration rules
# (privileged containers, hostNetwork/hostPID/hostIPC, dangerous Linux
# capabilities, hostPath/docker.sock mounts, etc.) remain strictly enforced.
#
# Deferred to a dedicated manifest-hardening PR (to avoid conflicting with
# in-flight workload manifest updates):
# - KSV-0014: readOnlyRootFilesystem=true requires explicit emptyDir volume
#   mounts for Spring Boot/Tomcat (/tmp), Flyway, and the Alpine pg_dump
#   backup CronJob (which runs `apk add` at container startup).
KSV-0014
AVD-KSV-0014

# - KSV-0118: explicit pod/container securityContext overrides; underlying
#   application images (distroless / Docker Hardened Images) already run as
#   non-root users by image default, while backup-cronjob currently requires
#   root at startup for `apk add`.
KSV-0118
AVD-KSV-0118
